Subject: [PATCH 5/6] scripts+docs: flag-consumer A/B harness and the
 2026-09-13 follow-up

A soundness fix to a peephole is only half a fix if it silently costs code
quality, so the measurement that justified this delivery's flag walk is checked
in rather than described: identity per TU, the two fold counts the SF guard
licenses (`testb $`, `cmpb $0`), emitted instruction count, and compile time
paired and interleaved (both arms alternate every sweep, min and median
reported, because a sequential measurement of this same change first reported
+4.55% that pairing showed to be drift).

The follow-up records the adjudication of the PR #512 audit -- which findings
hold, which of its justifications do not, and what its failure mode generalised
to -- together with the three reproducers, the mutation matrix, the rejected
coarser fix and its numbers, and two pins that were vacuous as first written.
